<title>JAPAN: HORSE RACING-SINGSPIEL WINS JAPAN CUP.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-SINGSPIEL WINS JAPAN CUP.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singspiel, a four-year-old colt</p>
<p>ridden by Frankie Dettori, won the Japan Cup horse race at Tokyo</p>
<p>Racecourse over a distance of 2,400 metres (1.5 miles) on</p>
<p>Sunday.</p>
<p>1. Singspiel (ridden by Frankie Dettori)</p>
<p>2. Fabulous  La Fouine (Mikio Matsunaga)</p>
<p>3.  (dead-heat) Strategic Choice (Richard Quinn)</p>
<p>and  Helissio (Olivier Peslier)</p>
<p>Winning distances: nose, one and a quarter lengths,</p>
<p>dead-heat. 15 ran.</p>
<p>Winner owned by Sheikh Mohammed Al Maktoum and trained by</p>
<p>Michael Stoute at Newmarket in England.</p>
<p>Value to winner: 172 million yen ($1.54 million).</p>
<p>Tote returns to 100 yen stake:  Win 760: places Fabulous La</p>
<p>Fouine (360), Strategic Choice (560), Helissio (150).</p>
</text>
